    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="0852" n="818" xml:id="pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Conference files, lot 60 D 627, CF 203</note>
                <head>No. 356<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the
                        Ambassador to the Soviet Union (Bohlen)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1954-01-25">January 25,
                            1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <item>Participants: The Secretary of State</item>
                    <item>Mr. Charles E. Bohlen</item>
                    <item>Mr. Michael B. Lustgarten (Interpreter)</item>
                    <item>Mr. V.M. Molotov</item>
                    <item>Mr. Andrei Gromyko</item>
                    <item>Mr. O.A. Troyanovski (Interpreter)</item>
                </list>
                <p>During the meeting today the Secretary of State said he expected in a day or two
                    to have a talk with Mr. Molotov to pursue the procedural discussions in regard
                    to atomic energy,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d356-f1"/> to which Mr. Molotov replied
                    that he was ready.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles E. Bohlen</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
